# config/no-go-paths - directories agent work must never be dispatched into
# (matched by bin/fm-no-go-lib.sh, enforced by bin/fm-spawn.sh). Copy this into
# a local, gitignored config/no-go-paths and edit. One absolute path prefix per
# non-empty, non-comment line.
#
# Rules:
#   - a leading ~ or ~/ expands to $HOME
#   - trailing slashes are tolerated
#   - matching is on a path-component boundary, so /a/b blocks /a/b and /a/b/c
#     but never /a/bc
#   - a symlinked alias of a declared prefix is blocked too
#   - a non-empty line that is not an absolute path refuses the spawn as a
#     configuration error rather than being silently skipped
#
# An ABSENT config/no-go-paths means no restriction: every dispatch behaves
# exactly as it did without the file.
#
# Secondmate homes inherit this file from the primary, so a secondmate's own
# crewmates are held to the same boundary.
#
# Example: personal working copies kept for reading and tinkering, which no
# crewmate, scout, or secondmate may ever be dispatched into.
~/personal-checkouts
/Volumes/scratch/hand-edits
